DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     uuhhssooccttll is a small connection utility for Option N.V. devices that are
     based on Options packet interface and uses proprietary AT_* calls to es‐
     tablish connections.  The utility (tries to) configure both default route
     and name servers (_/_e_t_c_/_r_e_s_o_l_v_._c_o_n_f).

     By default uuhhssooccttll detaches from the terminal upon on a successful con‐
     nection, a few command-line options exists that allows this behavior to
     be changed.

     uuhhssooccttll attempts to find a usable controlling serial port based on the
     provided network interface.  If this fails you might specify a serial
     port manually.

